# Factory reset — fail closed, hard-delete only

**Symptom:** After **Factory reset**, the app returns to the welcome hub even when the wipe failed, or residents remain as soft-archived (`archived_at`) instead of deleted.

## Rule

| Path | Required |
|---|---|
| `AdminLayout` `handleResetOnboarding` | Navigate to `/admin/onboarding` **only** when `restartNewLandlordOnboarding().ok === true`. On failure: alert, clear reset guard, stay put. |
| Resident wipe in `resetOnboardingPortfolio` | Hard-delete via `deleteResidentsForLandlord`. On failure → `ok: false`. **Never** fall back to `archived_at`. |
| Post-wipe assert | Fail unless tickets, active runs, **properties, units, residents, vendors** are all 0. |
| `clearOnboardingPortfolioSession` | If `resetOnboardingPortfolio` fails → return `ok: false` (do not save a fake clean welcome draft). |
| Start setup (`beginOnboarding`) | Clear wizard snapshot + pass `extractionReview: null` so prior Fast Track draft is not re-persisted. |
| `archiveOrClearPriorOnboardingResidents` | Hard-delete only; never soft-archive on Start. |

## Autofix (Bugbot)

1. Remove unconditional `window.location.assign('/admin/onboarding')` after a failed or thrown reset.
2. Delete any `archived_at` soft-archive branch in factory-reset or Start prior-resident clear.
3. Do not `console.warn` + continue as success when portfolio wipe fails in session clear.
4. Assert portfolio roster counts (not only tickets/runs) before `ok: true`.
5. On Start, clear `wizardSnapshotRef` upload/extraction before `goTo`, and pass `extractionReview: null`.
6. Keep `reportFactoryResetFailureToUser` as the primary failure surface.

## Do not

- Soft-archive residents to “finish” a factory reset
- Hard-reload to the welcome hub when `ok: false`
- Treat delete `ok: true` alone as proof without asserting empty ops where already required
